    <!--
    XFTL's own strings in German (Deutsch): the translations of
    assets/lang/en.xml, which the game shows on top of vanilla's
    data/text-de.xml. Any string missing here is shown in English.

    Write each one as en.xml has it, with the same name:
        <text name="xftl_button_back">...</text>
    Leave out the xftl_select_datafile_* and xftl_screen_small_* strings:
    they're shown before the game has FTL's fonts, in one with only English
    letters, so they stay in English.

    - Keep the placeholders \1, \2 and \3: the game puts a number or a
      name in their place. They can move within the sentence.
    - \n is a line break. Keep the ones in short texts (such as the
      confirmation boxes), which are laid out by hand.
    - Escape & as &amp;, < as &lt; and > as &gt;.
    - Only use characters FTL's fonts have: the Latin letters with accents
      and the Cyrillic alphabet are fine, but not typographic quotes,
      apostrophes and dashes (use " ' and -), nor the ellipsis (use ...).
    - The buttons and titles have a fixed size: keep them about as long as
      the English. The ones in capitals are in capitals in the game too.
    - Use the words vanilla FTL's own German uses (data/text-de.xml in
      ftl.dat), for the systems, races, resources and so on.

    Check it with: python3 tools/check_translations.py de
    (see doc/tools/translations.md, which also has a list of the missing ones
    to start from).
    -->


